<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">keeneye</ansi>

Keen Eye is a rogue's and a gryphon rider's skill: an eye for the door behind the tapestry
and the gap in the hedge. When your company walks into a room with a
secret exit it hasn't found, its best spotter looks once.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The odds</ansi>

  A spotter finds it when (level x 20) + (Perception / 4) + a roll of
  1 to 100 reaches 100. A level-4 rogue almost always does; with no
  rogue, your own eye still has a small chance (Perception alone).

Once found, a secret exit is yours to keep: it shows in that room's
exits for you from then on, after a restart too. Having been through it
already shows it as well.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  There is no command: it happens as you walk.
  <ansi fg="command">autoskill keeneye off</ansi> stops it (and your own chance with it).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help specialists</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help exits</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help autoskill</ansi>.
